draft: true
id: E555
title: Conan cross-build test_package must guard target execution with can_run
scope: conan test_package cross compile ohos windows self.run ctest
symptoms: A Conan test_package builds an OHOS executable but cmake.test mixes build and run environment wrappers or tries to execute an arm64 binary on Windows.
root_cause: Conan's build and run environments are different for cross compilation; the target executable is not runnable on the build host even when compilation and linking pass.
repair: Build the consumer normally, use an explicit self.run call for the L0 contract, and return after a can_run(self) guard when the host cannot execute the target. Run the same consumer on the authorized target device separately.
verification: TinyXML OHOS test_package built the arm64 consumer and recorded the guarded cross-run warning; the Windows host profile executed the same consumer and returned `tinyxml consumer PASS`.
boundaries: The guard prevents a false host failure only; it does not mark target execution PASS, and target W3 must retain its own signed binary, endpoint, RC, and cleanup evidence.
